course: dictionary
lesson: 6278
title: Monoxide and the word mono
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A long word can be made of smaller parts, and those parts give clues. In «carbon monoxide», mono means one, so a monoxide has one atom of oxygen joined to another element.
explain: Read this: «Carbon monoxide is a poisonous gas with no colour and no smell, so homes with fuel-burning heaters or boilers need a carbon monoxide alarm.» You cannot see, smell or taste the gas, so the sentence tells you why it is dangerous and why a home needs an alarm.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «If a carbon monoxide alarm goes off, get everyone out into fresh air.» An alarm that warns about carbon monoxide fits the sentence perfectly, so you have understood the phrase.
fact: Mono means one, so a monoxide has one atom of oxygen.
fact: Carbon monoxide is a poisonous gas with no colour, no smell and no taste.
fact: It can come from faulty boilers, gas fires, stoves, car exhausts and barbecues used indoors.
fact: If a carbon monoxide alarm beeps, open the windows, get everyone outside and call for help.
fact: Never use a barbecue inside a tent or room.
exercise: «Carbon monoxide is a poisonous gas with no colour and no smell.» Why do homes need a carbon monoxide alarm? | *Because you cannot see or smell the gas, so an alarm warns you | Because it is a type of food | Because the gas smells of roses | Because it makes a loud noise all day
exercise: In science, what does mono mean? | *One | Hot | Many | Two
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Never use a stove, heater or barbecue inside a tent, because of fire and carbon monoxide, a poison gas you cannot smell.» that means something that can harm you. | tent | stove | *poison | barbecue
test: «Some gases you smell, like rotten eggs, but some, like carbon monoxide from engines, have no smell at all.» What does this tell you about carbon monoxide? | It smells of rotten eggs | It only happens in tents | *It has no smell, so you cannot tell it is there by smell | It is a food that people eat
test: A monoxide has how many atoms of oxygen? | Two | None | *One | Three
exam: «If a carbon monoxide alarm goes off, or everyone gets headaches and feels dizzy, what should you do?» | Wait a day to see if it stops | Light a barbecue to warm the room | *Open the windows, get everyone into fresh air and call for help | Ignore it and go back to sleep
